# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Anything prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ ships to
# the client — keep secrets out of NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars.

# Auis dot — the floating shortcut menu in the bottom-right corner (Review /
# Edit / State modes, agent toggles). Hide it without disabling the shortcuts:
#NEXT_PUBLIC_AUIS_DOT_DISABLED=true

# Review Bridge — serverless, embedded in the Next app (/api/review-bridge/*),
# persisted to review-bridge/data/*.json. `npm run dev` already brings it up:
# no server, no port, no token.
#
# Optional: a shared secret for agents calling the bridge from outside the
# browser (skills, the dispatcher). Requests carrying it in the
# `x-bridge-agent-token` header are treated as an agent session. Only matters
# once you put Auis behind an auth layer (see app/api/review-bridge/_session.ts).
#BRIDGE_AGENT_TOKEN=
#
# Optional: where the bridge keeps its pre-write snapshots
# (default: ~/.auis/review-bridge-backups).
#REVIEW_BRIDGE_BACKUP_DIR=

# Review Mode — voice transcription and comment suggestions (OpenAI). Used only
# on the server by /api/review/transcribe and /api/review/suggest; it is never
# exposed to the browser. Without it, voice and suggestion actions stay hidden
# while the rest of Review Mode continues to work.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
